teration. We point have"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"We test IrAA with no preconditioner and with the ES preconditioner (corresponding to Rel1_x_n1O.1E10) described above. The IrAA parameters used are the following TOL = = 0.9,Q 0.125h2 (un-preconditioned case and Q = 0.1 (preconditioned case; no scheduling is used) . In all experiments we use a rank 1 matrix with Frobenius norm around 1 10-6 .","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":438.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":71.0,"r":541.0,"t":486.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,344],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/9","text":"We test IrAA with no preconditioner and with the ES preconditioner (corresponding to Rel1_x_n1O.1E10) described above. The IrAA parameters used are the following TOL = = 0.9,Q 0.125h2 (un-preconditioned case and Q = 0.1 (preconditioned case; no scheduling is used) . In all experiments we use a rank 1 matrix with Frobenius norm around 1 10-6 ."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"The results in Figure 11 display the numerical solutions obtained by IrAA methods with and without the ES preconditioner. In particular, both methods obtain visually similar numerical results in terms of solution contours and column and rOW index section for the final iterates The un-preconditioned IrAA gives a montonically increasing intermediate ranks. The ES-preconditioned IrAA converges very rapidly in 8 iterations","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":379.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.33333333333333,"r":542.3333333333334,"t":438.3333333333333},"charspan":[0,422],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/10","text":"The results in Figure 11 display the numerical solutions obtained by IrAA methods with and without the ES preconditioner. In particular, both methods obtain visually similar numerical results in terms of solution contours and column and rOW index section for the final iterates The un-preconditioned IrAA gives a montonically increasing intermediate ranks. The ES-preconditioned IrAA converges very rapidly in 8 iterations"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"FIG 11. Bratu problem solved by lrAA. The left figure displays the contour levels of the converged solution along with markers at the intersection points of the final inder sets I and J with and without ES preconditioner) The right figure displays the singular values from lrAA solutions and without the ES preconditioner. The bottom left figure and right figures display the rank evolution and the of the residual throughout the IrAA iterations for lrAA with and without the ES preconditioner top with top decay","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":71.33333333333337,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":71.33333333333333,"r":541.6666666666666,"t":119.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,512],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/11","text":"FIG 11. Bratu problem solved by lrAA. The left figure displays the contour levels of the converged solution along with markers at the intersection points of the final inder sets I and J with and without ES preconditioner) The right figure displays the singular values from lrAA solutions and without the ES preconditioner. The bottom left figure and right figures display the rank evolution and the of the residual throughout the IrAA iterations for lrAA with and without the ES preconditioner top with top decay"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"102","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":358.6666666666667,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":317.3333333333333,"r":329.3333333333333,"t":368.0},"charspan":[0,3],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/12","text":"102"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"no","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":353.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":396.3333333333333,"r":403.6666666666667,"t":358.3333333333333},"charspan":[0,2],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/tex